WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.840
May we then move on?

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:20.860
I think this is a paper which picks up a number
of the themes on which we have just been focused.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.570
Thank you very much, Chair.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:28.980
In taking these three subjects together, we
are emphasising the opportunity for better

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:35.290
alignment between the mandate, NHS planning
and the way in which we assess local health

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.290
systems.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.070
A few observations, first, on the mandate.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:44.579
Compared to the current mandate, it is shorter
and clearer.

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:48.670
Secondly, it reflects the Forward View.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:57.710
Thirdly, it helpfully includes a stronger
focus on long-term objectives for 2020, and

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:03.420
these objectives are phased in a way that
is consistent with the Spending Review.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:10.990
Fourthly, note that it sets objectives for
the wider NHS system, including other arm’s-length

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:20.820
bodies, so it is not just a mandate in respect
of NHS England’s own narrow functions.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:27.090
The planning guidance will reflect the mandate
and give expression to it.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:33.680
It is a shared endeavour with our arm’s-length-body
partners, including of course but not limited

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.380
to NHS Improvement.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:44.689
Our aspiration is for the core planning guidance
to be the shortest ever, and I can confirm

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:50.350
that we are on track to achieve this.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:59.340
Perhaps the most significant point is that
we are going to be emphasising local system

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:09.610
leadership, and the primacy of planning by
place rather than by individual institution.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:18.980
We are looking for two plans: a strategic
whole-system sustainability and transformation

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:28.080
plan for the period of October 2016 to March
2021, for agreement by NHS England and NHS

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:39.720
Improvement by July of next year, intended
as a local blueprint for delivering the Forward

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:49.920
View and achieving financial stability; and
then a second plan, which is the 2016/2017

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:56.790
operational plan by individual organisation.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:03:07.420
To emphasise the salience of those strategic
plans, and also to achieve some greater coherence

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:15.040
between different vertical national programmes
within a place, we are intending that the

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:25.920
quality of the sustainability and transformation
plans will determine the phasing of transformation

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:33.280
funding for 2017/2018 onwards.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:42.400
The final point I would make on the planning
guidance is that we will seek to set out a

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:50.820
short list of national ‘must-dos’ for
2016/2017.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:04:03.109
Finally, we will look to align the way we
assess CCGs, and indeed local health systems,

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:13.510
through a revised local health system improvement
and assessment framework, which has been referred

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:15.750
to as a CCG scorecard.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:22.410
We will be looking to finalise that with our
partners – we are developing it with CCGs

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:31.540
and the full range of other stakeholders – and
to consult on that in January of next year.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.490
I invite the Board to consider the proposed
approach that we are taking.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.120
Thank you very much, Ian.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.061
May I invite questions and comments to Ian?

00:04:39.061 --> 00:04:46.910
Ian, we have talked in this forum and others
about the significance to the Five Year Forward

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:52.720
View over the next five years of implementing
the vanguards, the pioneers and the new models

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:53.730
of care.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:59.760
I am curious as to what the planning guidance
will say, given that this is the first time

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:05.310
they are being asked to plan five years ahead,
to all those places in the country that are

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:15.900
not a vanguard, not a pioneer and not yet
a place where there is an active transformational

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.890
initiative of that kind.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:24.060
Because that is the majority of the country,
in fact; a majority of places are not vanguards

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.450
as yet.

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:29.530
What is the planning guidance going to say?

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:36.500
Is it going to ask those places to be aggressive
in their consideration of how they might become

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:44.731
aligned to new models of care, or is it going
to be silent on that question?

00:05:44.731 --> 00:05:45.731
Thank you, Noel.

00:05:45.731 --> 00:05:47.290
That is a very important question.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:55.770
I think at the heart of the local sustainability
and transformation plans is: what does this

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.560
mean for your local geography?

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.300
What is the overall shape of services?

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:05.420
There is an element here of describing the
plane as well as some of the component parts

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:11.100
of the plane, whether that is the mental health
piece or implementing the Cancer Taskforce.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:20.310
We are asking all systems to think through
how they wish to implement the new care models.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:28.570
To go back to my earlier comment on the objectives
within the mandate and the phasing of the

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:35.110
Spending Review, we also need to recognise
that there are some aspects of transformation

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:46.500
funding which will not be sufficient to achieve
full national roll out by 2020/2021.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:51.370
For example, in line with the statement in
the Forward View itself that the majority

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:56.790
of the country could be covered by new care
models within that period, that statement

00:06:56.790 --> 00:07:04.590
is reflected as part of the 2020 objectives
in the mandate, and in turn will be reflected

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.590
here.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:12.380
So there will be some parts of the country
that will be able to go faster and receive

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:17.080
greater central funding than others.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.680
It is a minuscule point but, of course, if
you are not a pioneer and you are not a vanguard,

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:25.280
it does not mean that you are not doing new
models of care and transformation.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:32.919
Indeed, many parts of the country are cracking
on with this.

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:40.760
I am always surprised, very pleasantly, by
the number of unofficial vanguards who are

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:44.190
making very good progress right across the
country.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:54.110
I think we can say, in relation to these documents,
that the mandate is now turning into a document

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:56.440
that can be meaningful for us.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:04.900
Secondly, it is the product of a highly iterative
process across Government, and between us

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:05.900
and Government.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:06.900
Productive?

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.090
Well, mainly productive.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.580
I think there has been some settlement.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:16.900
It has compelled the settlement and the crystallisation
of a number of key points about accountability

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.419
and responsibility and ambition.

00:08:19.419 --> 00:08:24.780
I think we should certainly, as a Board, welcome
the mandate that we now have in its current

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:25.780
form.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:28.520
So far as planning guidance is concerned,
the Board is going to need to give a lot of

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:33.380
further attention to the detail of the planning
guidance, and we will work further on that

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.440
prior to its publication.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:39.830
Can I invite any other comments or questions
to Ian on this item?

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:46.910
The only comment I would make, which again
is not [inaudible] in the sense that it is

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:52.339
evidence of action, the right rhetoric and
the right processes in place, hopefully going

00:08:52.339 --> 00:08:55.490
to drive the right behaviours, which I think
is the major challenge.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:09:05.890
My mind turns to outcomes and what mechanisms
we are putting in place to ensure that the

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:13.480
outcome of this is not just plans, but actually
some shift in what people receive in terms

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:16.270
of health and social care.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:22.150
That seems to me to be a significant new challenge
in terms of planning guidance that meets the

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:26.880
mandate, but then knowing that we have actually
pulled it all together in some way.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.460
It seems like we have work to do there.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:38.150
I might be wrong, but it seems fairly clear
to me.

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:39.740
Absolutely, Victor.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:44.290
Achieving a coherent plan is only part of
the story.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:49.210
I think we also need to emphasise to local
systems: ‘Do not think that you cannot make

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:56.570
progress now, before July, in cracking on
and doing the things that you were planning

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.850
to do anyway.’

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:04.339
There is further work that we are intending,
across NHS England and with our partners,

00:10:04.339 --> 00:10:14.730
on what the milestones and the actions set
out in the plans will be, and then how local

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:20.649
systems can be confident that they are making
progress towards their goals and that the

00:10:20.649 --> 00:10:26.310
implementation of those plans is having an
effect on outcomes, including in relation

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:30.420
to tackling local inequalities in their area.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:31.420
Right.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.250
Well, thank you.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:38.710
On that basis, could I ask the Board first
of all to endorse the general approach that

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:45.250
is outlined in Ian’s paper and in his presentation,
and secondly to delegate to the Chief Executive

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:50.130
and me the authority to finalise the form
of the planning guidance?

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:54.620
Which we obviously have to do in consultation
and with the agreement of the other arm’s-length

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:59.680
bodies, because this is a pan-arm’s-length-body
planning guidance, as it has been in previous

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:00.680
years.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.339
Are colleagues content to do that?

00:11:03.339 --> 00:11:04.339
Good.

00:11:04.339 --> 00:11:04.440
Thank you very much.

